Now compose the plan-stage handoff in Hindi/Hinglish (matching researcher's language), with three parts: inspection findings, proposed approach outline, assumptions & uncertainties.

Key design thinking:

Task question: "Do labels cleaned by Docta show higher credibility — reflected in improved predictive performance — vs raw labels, validated by both ChatGPT and in-house human annotators when the two sets disagree?"

Design outline:

Data setup (assumed, since repo empty):
- Instance set X (e.g., documents/texts), with label sets: Y_raw (raw/noisy labels, e.g., from legacy pipeline, weak labels, OCR/keyword auto-labels), Y_docta (Docta-cleaned labels), Y_gpt (ChatGPT labels), Y_human (in-house annotator gold, ideally 2-3 annotators with agreement stats).

Arms:
A0: No-model reference arms — direct label quality: agreement of each label source with gold (human), Cohen's/Krippendorff's kappa, per-class precision/recall of label source treated as predictor of human gold. This is the "credibility" measure independent of downstream model.
A1: Train-on-raw (train with Y_raw on X).
A2: Train-on-Docta (same model/protocol, train with Y_docta).
