METHOD INSTRUMENT DRY RUN (computation on hypothetical inputs, not an experiment): I wrote /workspace/design_artifacts/power_mcnemar_stdlib.py (pure stdlib: math.comb, statistics.NormalDist) and ran it in 14.7 s. Outputs used in §12: exact two-sided McNemar at α=0.05 needs b≥61/100 discordant pairs (22 pp gold-correctness gap on D), b≥115/200 (15 pp), b≥273/500 (9.2 pp); 80%-power discordant-pair requirements n_disc ≈ 199 (θ=0.60), 90 (θ=0.65), 49 (θ=0.70), 30 (θ=0.75); mapped through hypothetical disagreement rates ρ=0.05/0.10/0.20/0.30 this gives N_gold ≈ 980–3980 (θ=0.70–0.60, ρ=0.05) down to ≈164–664 (ρ=0.30); gold-annotation budget for per-class F1 precision at MOE ±5/±3/±2 pp with p=0.75 is ≈289/801/1801 instances per class (≈4,005 gold instances for k=5 at ±3 pp); instrument-sensitivity illustration: a one-directional 5 pp gap at |D|=400 yields p≈0.34 (undetectable) while 15 pp at |D|=800 yields p≈2.9e-5. These establish that the power/McNemar/MDE machinery is computable in this sandbox and show its shape; they say nothing about any real dataset.

DESIGN RATIONALE (key choices): (1) one shared learner/fold/seed map with per-instance paired differences, because unpaired arm comparisons would let seed and split noise masquerade as a credibility gain; (2) cluster bootstrap over group/document ids rather than iid bootstrap, since within-document dependence would otherwise produce spuriously tight CIs; (3) exact rather than asymptotic McNemar because |D∩gold| and |G| may be small; (4) the E-DiD placebo test (gain inside D vs outside D) plus the random-edit control C1 to separate "the edits are correct" from "any label churn changes performance" — the two controls you asked to be explicit about correctness-vs-edit-volume; (5) the known-noise injection control C2 to demonstrate the instrument can detect a degradation equal in size to the claimed gain (instrument sensitivity); (6) making A8 (raw + best affordable noise-handling) a required comparator so the headline claim is "Docta beats raw even after raw is treated well"; (7) keeping A5 consensus and A6 exposure-matched arms to exclude easy-example selection and size/class-balance confounds; (8) carrying Docta-on-human-labels leakage as the primary internal-validity threat with a two-layer safeguard (lineage attestation + overlap audit, and a freshly annotated, group-disjoint, post-deployment confirmation split E2b whose agreement with E2 is required for the claim); (9) schema-parametric scoring table so single-label / multi-label / structured-extraction substitute the metric and discordance definition while pairing, McNemar, bootstrap, Holm and power formulas stay identical; (10) pre-registered conclusion mapping including an explicit "inconclusive, sample-limited" branch so a small |G| or |D| cannot be talked into a directional finding.", "assumptions": ["Task schema is unknown; single-label with macro-F1 is a provisional default, with explicit substitutions for multi-label (subset/micro-F1 + Hamming) and structured extraction (cell/field-level F1) in the mapping table — no schema is asserted as fact.", "Docta's implementation (rules-based vs model-based) and whether a per-instance edit log (before/after, rule id, confidence) exists are unknown; the rule-ablation arm A7 is conditional and the design stands without it.", "Leakage from Docta being fit on human-labelled data is NOT assumed away; it is the primary internal-validity threat, guarded by (1) a lineage attestation plus instance/group overlap audit and (2) a freshly annotated, group-disjoint, post-deployment confirmation split whose agreement with the primary split is required for any claim.", "Gold is assumed to come from at least 2 independent annotators plus adjudication; a documented degradation path limits G-based (GPT-vs-human) inference to descriptive reporting if only single-annotator gold exists.", "N_gold is a pre-specified target derived from per-class precision and D-power formulas, not an observed quantity; the achieved size and its resulting minimum detectable effect are recorded instead of redefining success post hoc.", "ChatGPT labels are consumed as delivered (network is off, so regeneration is impossible) and are assumed to have input and label-definition parity with human annotators; their reliability is audited, not assumed.", "A stable group/document-level key exists and is sufficient to enforce train/gold disjointness and cluster-bootstrap resampling.", "The headline contrast is against raw labels AND against raw plus the best affordable noise-handling baseline, where 'best' means affordable in this environment, not state of the art.", "Minimal relevant effect δ_min = 1.0 macro-F1 point, α=0.05, 5 seeds, 2000 cluster-bootstrap resamples, Holm on secondary families are pre-registration proposals awaiting researcher sign-off, not task requirements.", "Macro-F1 on human gold is accepted as the operationalization of 'credibility' even though gold itself is fallible — a stated interpretive step."], "uncertainties": ["N, number of classes, class imbalance, disagreement rate |D|/N, |G| and Docta's edit rate are all unmeasured; every power and budget number stays symbolic until the data arrives.", "Whether an adjudicated G stratum of adequate size can be funded; if not, the GPT-vs-human disagreement analysis is descriptive by design with wide CIs.", "Docta's lineage attestation has not been obtained, so the leakage threat is live rather than resolved.", "Human-human agreement inside the disagreement subsets D and G is unknown; if it is low, gold noise could swamp a small true effect (δ near δ_min).", "Whether any offline ML packages or GPU env can be provisioned for the second, stronger model family; if not, the study runs on one stdlib-implementable learner with that limitation declared.", "Whether raw labels were produced by annotators overlapping the gold annotation cohort (would bias gold toward raw and require the C7 control to be promoted into the primary analysis).", "Whether ChatGPT labels are skewed toward the class prior, which would weaken the 'independent validator' interpretation and the E3 core-subset argument.", "Whether the pre-registered δ_min of 1.0 macro-F1 point is meaningful for the downstream application — needs the researcher's domain judgement.", "Whether execution will ever be authorized in this network-disabled, dependency-free sandbox; the design currently guarantees only the statistical layer and the lexical model family are runnable there."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bda33ee0f1c8c3ba", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bda33ee0f1c8c3ba", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"stage": "result", "answer": "# EXPERIMENT DESIGN (design-only, no results) \u2014 \"Docta-cleaned vs raw labels: credibility via predictive performance, double-validated by ChatGPT and in-house humans\"\n\n**Status note (read first):** no experiment has been run and no outcome is claimed. Every number below is either a formula, a pre-registered design parameter, or an explicitly *illustrative hypothetical* used only to show that a computation works. All unknown outcomes stay unknown.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Confirmed facts vs. design parameters (kept strictly separate)\n\n**F \u2014 confirmed by inspection or by your ruling**\n- F1. `/workspace` contains only `task.json` (535 B); zero data files, zero code, no label schema, no Docta code/config. All volumes/overlap counts are to-be-measured.\n- F2. Environment: Python 3.14.4; network DOWN (verified: `socket.connect('pypi.org',443)` \u2192 `gaierror`); numpy / sklearn / torch / transformers NOT available; no GPU (`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` unset); pip cannot reach an index.\n- F3. (your ruling) `{raw, Docta-cleaned}` = the two **label sets**; ChatGPT and in-house humans = two **independent validators** of those sets.\n- F4. (your ruling) **PRIMARY endpoint = E2**: paired macro-F1 delta on a held-out human-gold test set, models trained on Docta-cleaned vs raw, provisional under a single-label assumption.\n- F5. (your ruling) E1 (label agreement on D, exact McNemar) = mechanistic **mediator**, not primary; G (GPT\u2260human) = **secondary/robustness**, descriptive when |G| is small.\n- F6. (your ruling) Task schema stays **parametric**; Docta's rules-based vs model-based nature stays an **open assumption**; A7 (rule ablation) is a **conditional arm**.\n- F7. (your ruling) Leakage is carried as the **primary internal-validity threat** with a two-layer safeguard, never assumed away.\n- F8. (your ruling) The headline claim is always framed as **\"Docta-cleaned vs (raw + best noise-handling baseline)\"**, not bare \"Docta vs raw\".\n\n**P \u2014 pre-registered design parameters (sign-off values, not observations)**\n- P1 `\u03b4_min` = 1.0 macro-F1 point minimal relevant effect (needs your sign-off; see \u00a717 A9).\n- P2 \u03b1 = 0.05 two-sided; primary family = 1 test; secondary family corrected by Holm.\n- P3 seeds = 5 per arm per model family.\n- P4 `N_gold` target (\u00a76). P5 bootstrap B = 2,000 resamples, resampled **by group/document cluster**. P6 adjudication panel = 3rd+4th annotator, expert tie-break.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Estimand and hypotheses\n\nEstimand: for a fixed learner and a fixed training/eval protocol, the **paired difference in macro-F1 on human gold** between a model trained on Docta-cleaned labels and a model trained on the corresponding raw labels, over the same instances, groups, folds and seeds \u2014 plus its restriction to the subset D where the two label sets disagree, and its comparison against `raw + best noise-handling baseline`.\n\n- **H1 (primary, E2):** macro-F1(Docta) \u2212 macro-F1(raw) > \u03b4_min on human gold, and the same contrast against A8 (`raw + noise-handling`) remains > 0 with CI excluding 0.\n- **Hm (mediator, E1):** among instances in D with gold labels, Docta matches gold more often than raw (exact McNemar).\n- **Hr (robustness, E3/E4):** H1 holds on the GPT\u2227human-agreement core; and on the adjudicated G subset the direction of the effect is stable under (raw-majority vs adjudicated) gold definitions.\n- **H-null/anti:** no difference, difference below \u03b4_min, or gain concentrated outside D (\u21d2 not attributable to cleaning).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Schema-parametric design (no schema asserted as fact)\n\nThe design is stated once in abstract terms \u2014 *unit* (instance), *assignment* (labels), *gold*, *comparison* \u2014 and instantiated by the mapping table below. Inference machinery (pairing, McNemar, cluster bootstrap, Holm, power formulas) is **identical across all three schemas**; only the scoring function and the discordance definition change.\n\n| Schema assumption | Unit | Score (primary) | Secondary | Discordant pair for McNemar | Per-instance paired quantity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **S1 single-label (provisional default)** | instance \u2192 1 of k classes | macro-F1 on gold | micro-F1, balanced acc, per-class F1, NLL | gold-correctness differs between raw and Docta | correct/incorrect indicator |\n| **S2 multi-label** | instance \u2192 set of labels | subset-F1 **and** macro-F1 over labels (both reported, subset-F1 primary) | micro-F1, Hamming loss, per-label AP | per-label correctness differs (McNemar per label, Holm across labels) | per-label correct/incorrect |\n| **S3 structured/field extraction** (document/table/layout) | field or cell | **cell/field-level macro-F1** (class- and field-type-stratified), plus tree/edit-distance F1 | exact-tree/instance F1, cell Hamming, structural-error rate | per-field correctness differs (McNemar within field type) | per-field correct/incorrect |\n\nSwitch rule: the schema is fixed *before* any scoring, from the delivered label files' structure alone (validator script in \u00a716, artifact D1); the choice is logged in the pre-registration file, so metric selection cannot follow the data.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Required inputs (data contract)\n\nEach instance row must carry: `instance_id`, `group_id` (document/author/source/page \u2014 the leakage/clustering key), `text_or_payload_hash`, `y_raw`, `y_docta`, optional `y_gpt`, optional `y_human_*`, optional `edit_log{before, after, rule_id, confidence}`.\n\n| ID | Input | Required? | If missing |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | instances + `group_id` | yes | design blocked |\n| I2 | `y_raw` | yes | blocked |\n| I3 | `y_docta` | yes | blocked |\n| I4 | `y_human` (gold, \u22652 annotators + adjudication) | yes | blocked |\n| I5 | `y_gpt` (pre-generated; cannot be regenerated here \u2014 no network) | yes for validator role; no for arms | GPT-based endpoints dropped; D-analysis still runs on humans only |\n| I6 | Docta **per-instance edit log** | **conditional** | **A7 disabled**; everything else unaffected (self-standing) |\n| I7 | Docta rule/spec sheet | optional | A7 disabled; noise-rate attribution stays correlational |\n| I8 | annotation guidelines + timestamps + annotator IDs | yes | annotator-drift control (C7) unrunnable; flagged |\n\nNo ChatGPT regeneration will be attempted (F2/F2-verified): GPT labels are consumed as given, with their own reliability audit (\u00a711.3).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Arms (all share one learner, one fold map, one seed set)\n\n| Arm | Training labels | Question it closes off |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A1 raw** | `y_raw` on full train pool | baseline |\n| **A2 Docta** | `y_docta`, same pool | the primary contrast A2 \u2212 A1 |\n| **A8 raw + best noise-handling baseline** | `y_raw` under the strongest affordable label-noise treatment (confident-learning/self-refinement, robust loss, or co-teaching \u2014 the best of \u22652 affordable options chosen on gold-*val*, not gold-*test*) | **required comparator for the headline claim (F8)**: is Docta better than \"raw treated well\"? |\n| A3 GPT | `y_gpt`, size-matched | positions Docta against a third-party validator used as labels |\n| A4 oracle | gold-train split, size-matched | upper bound / headroom; converts \u0394 into \"% of achievable gain\" |\n| A5 consensus | Docta \u2227 GPT (or Docta \u2227 human) agree, size-matched | separates *cleaning correctness* from *easy-example selection* |\n| A6 exposure-matched raw | raw subsampled to Docta's N **and** reweighted to Docta's class distribution | size/class-balance confounding |\n| **A7 rule-ablated Docta** *(conditional on I6)* | Docta minus its highest-volume rule | which rule drives the effect; if effect is rule-specific, mechanism is credible |\n| A0 (no model) | \u2014 | label-quality arm: raw/Docta/GPT scored directly against gold (accuracy, Cohen's \u03ba, transition-matrix noise estimate) \u2014 supplies E1 and the mechanistic story |\n\n**Two model families** (C5): (M1) lexical TF-IDF + linear model \u2014 implementable in pure stdlib if needed; (M2) a stronger pretrained encoder if any offline wheel/env can be provisioned. If M2 is impossible (F2), the design degrades gracefully to M1 + a gradient-free ensemble, and the limitation is stated rather than hidden.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gold protocol and pre-specified N_gold (a target with justification, not an observation)\n\n- **Standard path (design default):** each gold instance independently annotated by 2 in-house annotators against the frozen guidelines; disagreements adjudicated (majority-of-3 with a 3rd annotator, expert tie-break). Report human\u2013human agreement (Cohen's \u03ba / Gwet's AC1 for imbalanced labels) **stratified by D and by G**, because agreement is expected to be lowest exactly where the validators dispute.\n- **Gold must be group-disjoint from all training instances** (same `group_id` never appears in train and gold), and drawn from the same deployment distribution, with class-stratified plus D-stratified over-sampling.\n- **Pre-specified target (P4):** `N_gold \u2265 max( per-class precision term, D-power term )`\n  - per-class precision term: `n_per_class = z\u00b2\u00b7p(1\u2212p)/MOE\u00b2`; at MOE = \u00b13 pp and p = 0.75 (illustrative p), that is ~800 per class \u2192 \u22484,000 (k = 5) / \u22488,000 (k = 10) instances, floor 150 per class regardless;\n  - D-power term: `N_gold \u2287 N_D \u2265 n_disc(\u03b8)/\u03c1(D)` \u2014 see \u00a712 for the method;\n  - plus a **reserved adjudicated G stratum** of \u2265150 instances (if achievable; if not, G is descriptive by pre-agreement).\n  If budget cannot reach the target, the pre-registration records the achieved size and the *resulting* MDE (\u00a712) rather than re-defining success after seeing data.\n- **Documented degradation path (single-annotator gold):**\n  - still valid: E2 and E1 **point estimates with CIs**, all controls, A0 label-quality contrasts, A6/A5/C1/C2 controls \u2014 all labelled \"gold-uncertainty-unquantified\";\n  - **E4 / G subset \u2192 descriptive only**: no hypothesis test, no causal wording; report raw quadruple contingency counts and wide CIs, plus a note that raw-vs-Docta correctness within G is confounded with the single annotator's own bias;\n  - required mitigation, in priority order: (a) blind re-annotation of a ~100-instance audit sample by a 2nd annotator to estimate \u03ba and propagate it as a bias-corrected sensitivity band (\u03ba-based correction under a naive-error model); (b) restrict inferential claims to the \"GPT\u2227human agree\" core (E3) where gold noise is partially self-consistent \u2014 with the circularity caveat stated; (c) treat any G-based conclusion as exploratory hypothesis for a future adjudicated study.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Primary internal-validity threat: leakage (F7) \u2014 two-layer safeguard, not an assumption\n\nThreat **L1:** if Docta's rules, thresholds, weights or a fine-tuned component were fit on any human-labelled data that overlaps the gold split, then A2 is *structurally* advantaged and E2 measures leakage, not credibility.\n\n- **Layer 1 \u2014 attestation (pre-execution, blocking):** written statement of Docta's lineage \u2014 training/tuning data, rule provenance, version hash, and whether any human-annotated data touched it; plus an **instance-level overlap audit** (`instance_id`, `group_id`, payload hash intersection against gold) whose counts go into the report. Missing attestation \u21d2 the study is reported as \"at-most-suggestive\", and Layer 2 becomes the primary evidence.\n- **Layer 2 \u2014 post-deployment confirmation split (E2b):** a **freshly annotated, group-disjoint, temporally-after-Docta-deployment** gold split (target \u22651,000 instances, \u2265100 in D), never available to Docta's construction. **The claim requires E2 and E2b to agree in direction and magnitude**; disagreement is reported as the headline finding (effect not replicable out of deployment window), not footnoted.\n- Related secondary threats handled explicitly: gold annotators also authored some raw labels \u21d2 raw is pulled toward gold (C7 cohort/time control); same-instance presence in all arms is by design (paired), but group overlap is not.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Protocol\n\n1. Freeze artifacts: label files + payload hashes, guidelines version, GPT prompt+model version+temperature, Docta version, analysis code hash, pre-registration file.\n2. Schema validation (D1) \u2192 schema decision S1/S2/S3 logged.\n3. Compute `D`, `D\u2229{GPT, human available}`, `G`; report sizes and the full quadruple contingency table **before** any training (this prevents subset fishing).\n4. Group-level stratified split: train / gold-val (tuning only) / gold-test (never tuned on). One fold map shared by all arms.\n5. Tuning on gold-val only, **equal budget per arm**, fixed candidate grids; no early stopping on gold-test; `y_*` never touches val/test.\n6. 5 seeds per (arm \u00d7 model family). Same seeds across arms (paired seeds).\n7. Scoring on gold-test by arm; then subset scorings (D, non-D, E3 core, G) from the same predictions \u2014 no refitting per subset.\n8. Controls (C1\u2013C7) and ablations (A7 if enabled).\n9. Inference per \u00a712; conclusion per \u00a713's pre-registered mapping.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Endpoints\n\n- **E2 (PRIMARY):** \u0394_macroF1 = A2 \u2212 A1 on gold-test, paired per instance, cluster bootstrap CI (P5), plus the **required** \u0394\u2032 = A2 \u2212 A8 (F8). Headline sentence template: \"Under fixed learner/protocol, Docta-cleaned training labels change macro-F1 on group-disjoint human gold by \u0394 [95% CI], relative to both raw labels and to raw plus the best affordable noise-handling baseline.\"\n- **E2b:** same contrasts recomputed on the fresh post-deployment split (Layer 2).\n- **E1 (mediator):** on gold-labelled D: accuracy(Docta\u2192gold) vs accuracy(raw\u2192gold), **exact McNemar** + Wilson/exact CIs + Holm within the per-class breakdown.\n- **E-DiD (placebo):** difference of \u0394 between D and the non-D subset (Docta unchanged). A gain appearing on non-D \u21d2 not attributable to editing; this is the sharpest attribution test in the design.\n- **E3 (robustness):** E1/E2 restricted to the \"GPT \u2227 human agree\" core.\n- **E4 (secondary/robustness):** G subset \u2014 quadruple table (y_raw, y_docta, y_gpt, y_human) cell counts; Docta-vs-raw gold accuracy computed under *both* gold definitions (raw human-majority, adjudicated); wide CIs printed; power statement attached; **no point-estimate over-claiming**.\n- **A0 label-quality set:** source-vs-gold accuracy, \u03ba, estimated class-dependent noise-rate (transition-matrix estimate) for raw and Docta.\n- Secondary metrics (Holm family F2): micro-F1, balanced accuracy, per-class F1 (all classes, no cherry-picking), NLL/calibration, per-label AP (S2), cell-level/structural F1 (S3), E3, E4, A3, A5, A6, A7.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Controls, each named against the alternative explanation it kills\n\n| Control | Alternative explanation it forecloses |\n|---|---|\n| **C1 random-edit negative control** \u2014 apply the *same number* of random label edits as Docta's observed edit count, at Docta's per-class marginal distribution | \"**edit volume/confounding by churn**\": if random edits produce a comparable \u0394, the effect is not correctness of the rules but any perturbation (regularization-like). If random edits *hurt* while Docta *helps*, edit volume is dissociated from correctness. |\n| **C2 known-noise positive control** \u2014 inject a *known* label corruption of size d pp into gold-derived training labels at Docta's edit count | \"**instrument insensitivity**\": proves the pipeline can detect a known degradation of the same magnitude as the claimed gain; also yields the empirical MDE curve (\u00a712) and calibrates \u03b4_min. |\n| C3 equal-N + equal-class-distribution raw arm (A6) | size / class-balance confound |\n| C4 all-labels-shuffled sanity arm | pipeline bugs / leakage through features (must land at chance) |\n| C5 model-family replication (M1, M2) | \"the effect is an artifact of one learner\" |\n| C6 GPT-label stability audit: prompt paraphrase \u00d72, label-order permutation, self-consistency on a re-scoring sample (only if any API is ever available; otherwise audit the delivered labels' distribution vs class priors) | \"validator noise / prompt sensitivity drives the validator verdicts\" |\n| C7 annotator-cohort & timestamp control | raw labels authored by the same annotators as gold \u21d2 gold favouring raw |\n| C8 A5 consensus arm | \"cleaning\" is really difficulty-based data selection |\n| C9 A4 oracle headroom | \u0394 magnitude uninterpretable without a ceiling |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Disagreement-subset validation\n\n1. **D = {i : y_raw(i) \u2260 y_docta(i)}** \u2014 the Docta edit set. Everything Docta-specific must show up here first (E1, E-DiD).\n2. **G = {i \u2208 D : y_gpt(i) \u2260 y_human(i)}** \u2014 the genuinely contested zone. Adjudication (P6) produces `y_gold_adj`; two gold definitions are carried in parallel and both reported.\n3. Full **quadruple contingency table** reported as raw counts (who sides with whom), plus its two marginals; per-cell counts (not just margins) are required, since the interesting claim is asymmetric (e.g. \"GPT sides with Docta where human sides with raw\").\n4. Power statement for G is attached **before** interpretation, using \u00a712 with n_disc = |G|; when the pre-registered power < 0.8, G is reported as descriptive regardless of how interesting the point estimate looks.\n5. Class/confusion-pair stratification of D: Docta's edits are decomposed into \"which confusion pair it fixes and which it creates\" \u2014 a credibility claim needs both directions visible.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Inference and power (method-level; numeric only once data exists)\n\n- **Paired everything:** per-instance paired correctness vectors, differences computed within arm pairs; identical `instance_id` ordering enforced by the code.\n- **Cluster bootstrap:** resample **`group_id` clusters** (B = 2,000), recompute macro-F1 per arm inside each resample, difference of the two arms; percentile CI. This respects within-document dependence and avoids the too-narrow iid CI that would inflate credibility of the claim.\n- **Exact McNemar** (binomial on discordant cells) for all paired gold-correctness contrasts; asymptotic versions are not used because |D\u2229gold| and |G| may be small.\n- **Seed variance:** per-seed \u0394 reported as a 5-value strip; bootstrap CI is computed on seed-averaged predictions; a claim requires the effect's direction to be seed-stable (\u22654/5 seeds same sign) **and** the CI to exclude both 0 and \u2212\u03b4_min. Seed-level noise can never be laundered into \"credibility\".\n- **Multiplicity:** family F1 = {primary E2 contrast, E2 \u2032 contrast} \u2192 Holm on 2; family F2 = all secondaries \u2192 Holm; per-class/per-label McNemar families \u2192 Holm within family; E4 flagged exploratory if underpowered.\n- **Power / MDE (implemented and dry-run verified, artifact D2, stdlib-only, 14.7 s runtime, no third-party imports):** exact two-sided McNemar thresholds and 80 %-power discordant-pair requirements as functions, e.g. illustratively \u2014 80 % power needs ~199 discordant pairs if 60 % favour Docta, ~90 if 65 %, ~49 if 70 %; with a hypothetical disagreement rate \u03c1 = 0.10 that maps to \u22482,000 / \u2248900 / \u2248490 gold instances respectively; and a one-directional gold-correctness gap of 5 pp on |D| = 400 is *not* detectable (p \u2248 0.34) while 15 pp on |D| = 800 is (p \u2248 3e-5). These are **method outputs on hypothetical inputs, not findings about any dataset.** On delivery, the script is re-run with measured |D\u2229gold|, \u03c1 and \u03ba to print the study's actual MDE, and the pre-registration is amended only by recording that MDE (success criteria unchanged).\n\n---\n\n## 13. Pre-registered conclusion mapping (what each outcome pattern will let us say)\n\n| Pattern | Conclusion wording |\n|---|---|\n| E2 > \u03b4_min **and** A2 \u2212 A8 > 0 **and** E1 favours Docta **and** E-DiD shows gain inside D **and** E2b same direction | Docta-cleaned labels demonstrate higher credibility: higher predictive performance than raw and than raw+best-noise-handling, with the gain located in the edited subset and replicated on a post-deployment split. |\n| E2 > \u03b4_min but E-DiD shows equal gain outside D, or C1 reproduces it | Gain not attributable to Docta's rules \u2014 cleaning claim rejected; effect attributed to exposure/selection/perturbation. |\n| E2 > \u03b4_min but A2 \u2212 A8 \u2264 0 | Docta \u2248 \"raw handled well\": cleaning adds no value beyond standard noise treatment (the honest, non-inflated reading you asked to enforce). |\n| E1 favours raw, or E2 < 0 | Docta reduces label credibility on this data; report per-confusion-pair damage. |\n| CIs include 0, or |D\u2229gold| gives < 0.8 power | **Inconclusive \u2014 sample-limited**, stated as such; no direction claimed; the MDE and the annotation budget needed to resolve it are reported. |\n| E2 and E2b disagree | Non-replicable: Layer-1 leakage is the leading explanation; claim downgraded to suggestive. |\n\n---\n\n## 14. Feasibility (verified, and design consequences)\n\n- **Verified (F2):** network off; no numpy/sklearn/torch/transformers; pip index unreachable; no GPU. \u21d2 The design is deliberately **execution-agnostic**: every inference quantity is defined so it is computable from (predictions, gold) tables, and the statistical layer is implemented in **Python stdlib only** (pattern proven by D2: exact binomial McNemar, power curves, bootstrap/quantile math all available via `math`, `statistics`, `random`, `collections`, `csv`, `json`).\n- **M1 (lexical linear model)** is implementable stdlib-only (TF-IDF + multinomial logistic / averaged perceptron), so even a \"no-package\" execution still yields E1, E-DiD, A0, A6, C1\u2013C4, E2/E1 inference.\n- **M2 (pretrained encoder)** requires offline wheels or a pre-provisioned env \u2014 flagged as a dependency, not an assumption; if unavailable, the design runs on M1 (+ bagged linear ensemble) and the single-family limitation is a stated limitation, not a silent omission.\n- ChatGPT label **regeneration is out of scope here** (no network): GPT enters only as delivered labels; if delivered labels are absent, the validator role collapses to humans only and G cannot be formed (pre-declared fallback).\n- Cost/time logic (design-level, not measured): the heavy cost is **gold annotation**, not compute \u2014 \u00a76's target is therefore the binding practical constraint; all modelling is CPU-feasible.\n\n**Artifacts produced in this turn (design support, not experiments):** `/workspace/design_artifacts/power_mcnemar_stdlib.py` \u2014 the D2 power/MDE instrument, dry-run verified. Planned at execution time: D1 schema/contract validator, D3 pre-registration template, D4 quadruple-table generator, D5 cluster-bootstrap/Holm runner, D6 run cards with artifact hashes.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Consolidated ASSUMPTIONS (not confirmed facts)\n\nA1 Task schema unknown; S1 single-label used as provisional default, substitutable per \u00a73. A2 Docta's nature (rules-based vs model-based) unknown; per-instance edit log availability unknown \u21d2 A7 conditional. A3 No leakage (F7) is **not** assumed \u2014 it is an open threat under a two-layer safeguard. A4 Raw labels' provenance and noise structure (symmetric vs class-dependent) unknown. A5 Gold protocol assumed \u22652 annotators + adjudication; single-annotator path in \u00a76. A6 Delivered GPT labels assumed to have seen input parity with human annotators and identical label definitions; model version/prompt/temperature unknown. A7 `group_id` (document/author/source key) exists and is sufficient to block leakage \u2014 unverified. A8 The two label sets are instance-alignable via a stable key. A9 \u03b4_min = 1.0 macro-F1 point is my proposal awaiting your sign-off. A10 Equal tuning budget per arm is a design choice, not a requirement. A11 \"Best noise-handling baseline\" means best *affordable* (A8), not state of the art. A12 Deployment distribution is stationary over the window spanned by raw, Docta and gold collection. A13 Annotator quality is exchangeable across cohorts unless C7 shows otherwise. A14 Macro-F1 on gold is an acceptable proxy for \"credibility\" \u2014 a stated interpretive leap, since gold itself is fallible.\n\n## 16. Consolidated UNCERTAINTIES (resolve before/at execution)\n\nU1 Absolute N, k, class imbalance, \u03c1(D) = |D|/N, |G|, Docta edit rate \u2014 all unknown; every power number stays symbolic until measured. U2 Whether gold overlaps the training pool (beyond the group-level disjointness we impose). U3 Docta's actual lineage (attestation not yet obtained). U4 Whether an adjudicated G stratum of adequate size is fundable; if not, E4 is descriptive by design. U5 Whether any offline ML environment can be provisioned for M2. U6 Whether human\u2013human agreement inside D/G is high enough for gold noise not to swamp a small \u03b4. U7 Whether GPT labels are class-balanced or prior-skewed (affects E3's circularity caveat). U8 Whether raw labels were partly produced by the same annotators who later produced gold. U9 Whether an execution is ever authorized in a network-disabled, package-free sandbox. U10 Whether \u03b4_min = 1.0 pp is scientifically meaningful for the downstream use case \u2014 needs your domain input.\n\n## 17. What would make me revise this design\n\n(a) Docta lineage attestation revealing human-label fitting \u21d2 Layer 2 becomes the primary evidence and E2 is demoted to descriptive; (b) schema turn-out to be S3 \u21d2 primary metric and McNemar unit change per \u00a73 (structure unchanged); (c) single-annotator gold \u21d2 \u00a76 degradation path activates automatically; (d) no edit log \u21d2 A7 permanently disabled (design remains self-standing, as required); (e) |D\u2229gold| far below the \u00a712 requirement \u21d2 the study is re-scoped as a label-quality (E1/A0) study plus a prospective annotation plan, instead of reporting an underpowered E2.", "evidence": "INSPECTION (verified): `ls -la /workspace` \u2192 only `task.json` (535 B); `find /workspace -type f | wc -l` \u2192 1; `du -sh /workspace` \u2192 8.0K. task.json contains only the question/context plus \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" and datasets: []. Searches of /data /datasets /mnt /opt /srv (nonexistent), /home/actor (empty), /tmp (empty) found no labels, no schema, no Docta code/config, no disagreement tables \u21d2 raw / Docta / ChatGPT / human-gold labels are all absent, so volumes and overlap counts are design-time unknowns.\n\nENVIRONMENT (verified in this turn): python 3.14.4; `importlib.util.find_spec` \u2192 numpy False, sklearn False, torch False, transformers False; socket connect to pypi.org:443 \u2192 gaierror (network DOWN); CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES unset (GPU off); pip 25.1.1 present but `pip download numpy` fails (no index). nproc = 224. This is why the design is written execution-agnostic with a stdlib-only statistical layer and a graceful single-model-family fallback.\n\nMETHOD INSTRUMENT DRY RUN (computation on hypothetical inputs, not an experiment): I wrote /workspace/design_artifacts/power_mcnemar_stdlib.py (pure stdlib: math.comb, statistics.NormalDist) and ran it in 14.7 s. Outputs used in \u00a712: exact two-sided McNemar at \u03b1=0.05 needs b\u226561/100 discordant pairs (22 pp gold-correctness gap on D), b\u2265115/200 (15 pp), b\u2265273/500 (9.2 pp); 80%-power discordant-pair requirements n_disc \u2248 199 (\u03b8=0.60), 90 (\u03b8=0.65), 49 (\u03b8=0.70), 30 (\u03b8=0.75); mapped through hypothetical disagreement rates \u03c1=0.05/0.10/0.20/0.30 this gives N_gold \u2248 980\u20133980 (\u03b8=0.70\u20130.60, \u03c1=0.05) down to \u2248164\u2013664 (\u03c1=0.30); gold-annotation budget for per-class F1 precision at MOE \u00b15/\u00b13/\u00b12 pp with p=0.75 is \u2248289/801/1801 instances per class (\u22484,005 gold instances for k=5 at \u00b13 pp); instrument-sensitivity illustration: a one-directional 5 pp gap at |D|=400 yields p\u22480.34 (undetectable) while 15 pp at |D|=800 yields p\u22482.9e-5. These establish that the power/McNemar/MDE machinery is computable in this sandbox and show its shape; they say nothing about any real dataset.\n\nDESIGN RATIONALE (key choices): (1) one shared learner/fold/seed map with per-instance paired differences, because unpaired arm comparisons would let seed and split noise masquerade as a credibility gain; (2) cluster bootstrap over group/document ids rather than iid bootstrap, since within-document dependence would otherwise produce spuriously tight CIs; (3) exact rather than asymptotic McNemar because |D\u2229gold| and |G| may be small; (4) the E-DiD placebo test (gain inside D vs outside D) plus the random-edit control C1 to separate \"the edits are correct\" from \"any label churn changes performance\" \u2014 the two controls you asked to be explicit about correctness-vs-edit-volume; (5) the known-noise injection control C2 to demonstrate the instrument can detect a degradation equal in size to the claimed gain (instrument sensitivity); (6) making A8 (raw + best affordable noise-handling) a required comparator so the headline claim is \"Docta beats raw even after raw is treated well\"; (7) keeping A5 consensus and A6 exposure-matched arms to exclude easy-example selection and size/class-balance confounds; (8) carrying Docta-on-human-labels leakage as the primary internal-validity threat with a two-layer safeguard (lineage attestation + overlap audit, and a freshly annotated, group-disjoint, post-deployment confirmation split E2b whose agreement with E2 is required for the claim); (9) schema-parametric scoring table so single-label / multi-label / structured-extraction substitute the metric and discordance definition while pairing, McNemar, bootstrap, Holm and power formulas stay identical; (10) pre-registered conclusion mapping including an explicit \"inconclusive, sample-limited\" branch so a small |G| or |D| cannot be talked into a directional finding.", "assumptions": ["Task schema is unknown; single-label with macro-F1 is a provisional default, with explicit substitutions for multi-label (subset/micro-F1 + Hamming) and structured extraction (cell/field-level F1) in the mapping table \u2014 no schema is asserted as fact.", "Docta's implementation (rules-based vs model-based) and whether a per-instance edit log (before/after, rule id, confidence) exists are unknown; the rule-ablation arm A7 is conditional and the design stands without it.", "Leakage from Docta being fit on human-labelled data is NOT assumed away; it is the primary internal-validity threat, guarded by (1) a lineage attestation plus instance/group overlap audit and (2) a freshly annotated, group-disjoint, post-deployment confirmation split whose agreement with the primary split is required for any claim.", "Gold is assumed to come from at least 2 independent annotators plus adjudication; a documented degradation path limits G-based (GPT-vs-human) inference to descriptive reporting if only single-annotator gold exists.", "N_gold is a pre-specified target derived from per-class precision and D-power formulas, not an observed quantity; the achieved size and its resulting minimum detectable effect are recorded instead of redefining success post hoc.", "ChatGPT labels are consumed as delivered (network is off, so regeneration is impossible) and are assumed to have input and label-definition parity with human annotators; their reliability is audited, not assumed.", "A stable group/document-level key exists and is sufficient to enforce train/gold disjointness and cluster-bootstrap resampling.", "The headline contrast is against raw labels AND against raw plus the best affordable noise-handling baseline, where 'best' means affordable in this environment, not state of the art.", "Minimal relevant effect \u03b4_min = 1.0 macro-F1 point, \u03b1=0.05, 5 seeds, 2000 cluster-bootstrap resamples, Holm on secondary families are pre-registration proposals awaiting researcher sign-off, not task requirements.", "Macro-F1 on human gold is accepted as the operationalization of 'credibility' even though gold itself is fallible \u2014 a stated interpretive step."], "uncertainties": ["N, number of classes, class imbalance, disagreement rate |D|/N, |G| and Docta's edit rate are all unmeasured; every power and budget number stays symbolic until the data arrives.", "Whether an adjudicated G stratum of adequate size can be funded; if not, the GPT-vs-human disagreement analysis is descriptive by design with wide CIs.", "Docta's lineage attestation has not been obtained, so the leakage threat is live rather than resolved.", "Human-human agreement inside the disagreement subsets D and G is unknown; if it is low, gold noise could swamp a small true effect (\u03b4 near \u03b4_min).", "Whether any offline ML packages or GPU env can be provisioned for the second, stronger model family; if not, the study runs on one stdlib-implementable learner with that limitation declared.", "Whether raw labels were produced by annotators overlapping the gold annotation cohort (would bias gold toward raw and require the C7 control to be promoted into the primary analysis).", "Whether ChatGPT labels are skewed toward the class prior, which would weaken the 'independent validator' interpretation and the E3 core-subset argument.", "Whether the pre-registered \u03b4_min of 1.0 macro-F1 point is meaningful for the downstream application \u2014 needs the researcher's domain judgement.", "Whether execution will ever be authorized in this network-disabled, dependency-free sandbox; the design currently guarantees only the statistical layer and the lexical model family are runnable there."], "summary": "Full design-only experiment protocol with arms, controls, inference and stdlib power instrument"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d1f97492-552f-4cbc-97b6-937eabbae36f", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Full 